From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:53:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] A lesson knows when its host arrived

A student who arrives first opens the room; that is not a teacher being
there. The host's own arrival is its own fact (lesson_host_join from the
room, or Daily's word for a participant who is not the student), and the
no-join sweep reads it, so a student waiting alone is finally a task.
With it, the stage's docs: the three cron jobs, the two push rows, the
lesson-room secrets, the runbook's new sections, and the lessons this
branch taught CLAUDE.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
