+## A lesson ended and no draft arrived
+
+**From your phone:** the teacher ended the lesson and never got "Your report draft is ready", or the draft is the heuristic one (`source = 'heuristic'`) on a project with a key set.
+
+**Developer, in order:**
+
+1. `select payload->>'error', at from public.lesson_events where kind = 'finalize_not_asked' order by at desc limit 5;` A row here means the database could not ask at all: `edge_config.functions_url` is unset or the Vault `service_role_key` is missing — the same two things every push depends on, so pushes will be failing too (see "Pushes are not arriving").
+2. Supabase → Edge Functions → **lesson-finalize** → logs. `unauthorised` (401) means the bearer the database sent is not the project's SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — the Vault row holds a stale key. `no such session` is a booking that was deleted between the end and the ask. `[edge] lesson-finalize <pass> fell back to the heuristic: http — 401` is a wrong ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; `… no_key` is an unset one; `… network — …` is a pass that timed out (110 s each) or could not reach Anthropic; `… parse — …` is a reply that was not the JSON asked for. Each of these costs that one pass only — the other two still land — and none throws the run away. `lesson-finalize/transcript` means Daily's access-link or download failed (DAILY_API_KEY, or the transcript id Daily sent): the lesson was finalised on the room's own segments and merges on the next `transcript` ask.
+3. `select source, rationale from public.lesson_report_drafts where session_id = '<id>';` `heuristic` with a key set and no log line means the family has no `ai_analysis` consent (`select kind, revoked_at from public.lesson_consents where student_id = '<student>'`); `select kind, model, at from public.ai_usage where session_id = '<id>'` says which calls were made at all.
+4. To run it again by hand, in the SQL editor: `select public.invoke_edge_function('lesson-finalize', jsonb_build_object('session_id', '<id>', 'reason', 'end'));` — idempotent: metrics, coaching and the draft are replaced, follow-ups are proposed only once, a replaced draft pushes nobody, and a lesson older than a day pushes nobody at all.
+
+## A lesson recording is still at Daily after its retention
+
+**Developer:** retention is two halves. `sweep_lesson_retention` (cron
+`mv-lesson-retention`) marks `lesson_recordings.deleted_at` once a recording is
+older than `retention_settings.recording_months`; `recordings-cleanup` (cron
+`mv-recordings-cleanup`, every half hour) deletes the bytes at Daily and stamps
+`purged_at`. Rows waiting between the two:
+
+```sql
+select session_id, deleted_at, purged_at, provider_recording_id
+  from public.lesson_recordings
+ where deleted_at is not null and purged_at is null
+ order by deleted_at limit 20;
+```
+
+A row older than an hour here means the function is not running: `cron.job`
+has no `mv-recordings-cleanup` (re-run the schedule block in DEPLOYMENT.md), or
+DAILY_API_KEY is not set — the function logs `recordings-cleanup has no
+DAILY_API_KEY set. Nothing is purged.` once and answers 503. A row whose
+`provider_recording_id` is null never had bytes at Daily and is nobody's job.
+A Daily refusal (401 is the key, 5xx is Daily) leaves the row for the next run
+and reaches the error sink under `recordings-cleanup`; Daily answering 404 is
+counted as purged, on purpose. Each run logs one line: `recordings-cleanup:
+purged N, kept M` and `, batch full` when fifty rows were waiting, so a backlog
+never reads as an all-clear.
+
+## A follow-up was approved and nobody heard
+
+**Developer:** the teacher's yes moves `lesson_followups.status` from proposed
+to approved and the push goes to the in-charge seats of the lesson's department
+— `department_members.is_incharge`, an office role, an open account — never to
+the whole zone and never to the teacher who said yes. A department with no
